Immix was the host of a talk show called the Lighthouse, and called himself the audience's stalwart host. On the show he spoke straight to whoever was watching, and beside him sat his silent aide, KiRiin, a [[Bestiary/Kaathe|Kaathe]] he introduced as the lovely KiRiin. The show played fanfares and projected illustrations behind Immix as he talked.

An aspect of Immix hosted from a studio, seated behind a dark wood desk while his guests shared a red velvet couch under a spotlight, KiRiin in a chair of its own. The one subject he would not discuss was the man downstairs.

The cycles of the world were taken over some time ago by an aspect of Immix and the nothing god of the [[Divinity/Thessians|Thessians]]. Immix knew which way the present cycle was going, and said on air that his days were numbered. He gave away his divinity, all of it, and he turned on a good friend for [[Divinity/Unknown Entities/The Deep|the Deep]].

The Lighthouse no longer held Immix. Since he gave his divinity away he could leave his stage and walk in the world, and he did, sitting on a panel of talk show hosts at [[Geography/Syrin (Locality)/Media Con|Media Con]] on [[Geography/Syrin (Locality)|Syrin]] and looking as he always had. He favored a tragic ending because a tragedy is tidy: everyone ends where they end, the audience sees it coming from far off and waits for it, and the anticipation is the best part. He called the work entertainment and claimed to be detached from the people who stepped onto his stage. The show reached [[Geography/Syrin (Locality)|Syrin]], where [[Org/Althane/The Weft|the Weft]] were known as its cast and their look was worn by cosplayers.

Immix had taken the third observation of the [[Divinity/Althane/The Observers|Observers]], where the previous third had stood.

In the last year of [[Geography/Althane/index|Althane]]'s cycle he kept an incomplete prison, and he waited there in several parts. Three of them fought side by side: a being that shaped spheres of creation and oblivion, one that wove words and suggestions into a hearer's mind, and a taller one of chains that rends souls. When two of the parts fell, the third wrapped itself in their remains and rose as one bright, many-armed figure with a great open chest and a mouth running down from the ribs, wings spread behind it. He called on holy light and struck with a holy bow and greatsword from a domain in which healing came at half strength, and healed himself from the wounds he dealt. [[People/Althane/Lev|Lev]] cut his wings away and put his blade through his head, and he died in the ruined arena.

Through the Weft's travels toward Oresk, an aspect of Immix kept summoning them in their dreams onto his talk show, "The Lighthouse, with an Aspect of Immix", and asked them pointed, needling, antagonistic questions about what they were doing and how they fought. He worked for [[Divinity/Althane/The Stranger|the Feep]].
